# 11b -- the import plan screen, and editing a row in place.
##
# The three row states, then `e` on the two kinds of row the earlier version
# refused to open at all: a READY row, and a row whose only business is
# creating something. The cursor starts on a ready one, so the first `e` a
# person ever pressed was the refused case.
e: e opens the ready row as the command it is
ctrl+w: ctrl+w takes back a token at a time
ctrl+w: .
ctrl+w: .
ctrl+w: .
ctrl+w: back to the destination
s: typing a new one
h: .
e: .
l: shel -- the completion is for `at`, so it offers Locations
tab: tab takes it
enter: enter re-checks the row
ctrl+n: .
ctrl+n: .
ctrl+n: .
ctrl+n: onto a row that would create an item
e: e opens that one too, which it would not before
esc: esc leaves the field and nothing else
